  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Tulsa Imperative** (1 review): Singled out as a rarity, with an amazing version and very energetic performance [4]\n- **Family Happiness** (1 review): Reviewer says the energy here ranks among his best recorded performances ever [4]\n- **Orange Ball Of Hate** (1 review): Reviewer considers this their favorite version of the song ever [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Raid On Entebbe**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **Tulsa Imperative**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **Orange Ball Of Love**: rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n- **Masher**: rare: 8 archived performances [5]\n- **West Country Dream**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n- **We Were Patriots**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Waving At You**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **I Corinthians 13:8-10**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mountaingoats1998-02-06.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 81 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer finds the recording quality wonderful for its age; Sound is good overall, but the first three songs are quite quiet, possibly just the reviewer's computer; Volume runs a bit low, but the recording is otherwise tremendous [2][3][4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mountaingoats1998-02-06.flac16**: taped by Jon Nall; transferred by Brian Eck; source: csb/mod-->d7 [1]",
